WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:20.407
next morning Ally was about to put on her meld medallion when Alpha chimed and her screen blinked

2
00:00:20.547 --> 00:00:23.730
on. "Alpha!

3
00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.331
You're recalibrated!"

4
00:00:25.771 --> 00:00:26.372
Ally cheered.

5
00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:30.936
"I cannot wait to get my powers back.

6
00:00:31.324 --> 00:00:32.784
It's no fun being a human.

7
00:00:33.485 --> 00:00:38.806
I can't read people's minds, and I've broken three plates here at home and lots of dishes at

8
00:00:38.846 --> 00:00:44.268
the diner, and I can't count fast or—" Alpha's screen had strange wavy lines.

9
00:00:44.288 --> 00:00:45.968
"Memory overload!

10
00:00:46.488 --> 00:00:47.949
Recalibration incomplete!

11
00:00:48.389 --> 00:00:50.129
Corrupted files must be deleted!"

12
00:00:50.149 --> 00:00:52.430
"Oh no."

13
00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:53.910
Ally's heart sank.

14
00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:55.991
"How long will that take?"

15
00:00:56.011 --> 00:01:00.212
"Unclear. Commencing shutdown to execute full repairs."

16
00:01:01.164 --> 00:01:03.885
Alpha's screen blinked off and then quickly back on.

17
00:01:03.905 --> 00:01:10.827
"Warning! Do not touch power sources until reboot is complete, or else complete system failure is assured!"

18
00:01:10.847 --> 00:01:15.468
"I won't touch anything until you're back to yourself," Ally said.

19
00:01:15.488 --> 00:01:16.729
"I promise."

20
00:01:18.629 --> 00:01:22.150
"Hurry up, Alpha," she thought as she put on her meld medallion.

21
00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.571
"Even though you can be really bossy, I miss you.

22
00:01:26.292 --> 00:01:27.252
And I need you!"

23
00:01:32.136 --> 00:01:34.077
It was a very busy morning at the diner.

24
00:01:34.098 --> 00:01:41.983
"It's like everyone in Sandville showed up for breakfast today," Ally said as she and Flo waited at

25
00:01:42.023 --> 00:01:43.644
the kitchen for their customers' orders.

26
00:01:43.664 --> 00:01:45.766
"You can say that again!"

27
00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:46.746
Ray huffed.

28
00:01:48.207 --> 00:01:50.349
"Why did I send Randy to work the food truck today?"

29
00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:54.031
"You had no choice," Flo said.

30
00:01:54.051 --> 00:01:57.574
"The truck was booked to serve food at Splash Town Park."

31
00:01:57.594 --> 00:01:59.235
"I know."

32
00:01:59.675 --> 00:02:00.656
Ray wiped his brow.

33
00:02:01.512 --> 00:02:03.033
"I just could use his help in the kitchen.

34
00:02:03.794 --> 00:02:04.574
Here's your order, Ally."

35
00:02:05.595 --> 00:02:09.137
Ally grabbed the two plates and hurried to deliver them to Phil and Tina.

36
00:02:09.157 --> 00:02:11.379
"Two breakfast sandwiches!"

37
00:02:11.399 --> 00:02:14.661
"Thanks, Ally," Phil said.

38
00:02:16.563 --> 00:02:20.205
While Ally refilled their coffee cups, Tina took a bite of her sandwich.

39
00:02:20.225 --> 00:02:24.308
"You're right, Phil," she said.

40
00:02:24.328 --> 00:02:28.251
"This is the best breakfast sandwich I've ever had!

41
00:02:28.271 --> 00:02:31.921
Say, how's your new computer, Ally?"

42
00:02:31.941 --> 00:02:35.023
"It's fine, thanks," Ally said.

43
00:02:35.903 --> 00:02:40.566
She wasn't sure why Tina was curious about her new computer, but Ally didn't really want to talk

44
00:02:40.606 --> 00:02:40.966
about it.

45
00:02:42.087 --> 00:02:46.250
She couldn't bear to think about what would happen if Alpha couldn't recalibrate successfully.

46
00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.371
"How much RAM does it have?"

47
00:02:49.812 --> 00:02:50.592
Tina asked her.

48
00:02:50.612 --> 00:02:53.154
"Ram?" Ally repeated.

49
00:02:53.174 --> 00:02:56.075
"I, uh—" Crash!

50
00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:00.741
"Gah!" The sound of pans crashing was followed by Ray yelling.

51
00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:02.681
Ally ran to the kitchen.

52
00:03:04.162 --> 00:03:05.462
"Ray! Are you all right?"

53
00:03:05.482 --> 00:03:08.963
"There are too many orders, and I can't keep up!"

54
00:03:09.523 --> 00:03:10.103
Ray moaned.

55
00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:13.004
"I've got to get Randy back here."

56
00:03:13.024 --> 00:03:16.745
"He just texted me," Flo said.

57
00:03:16.765 --> 00:03:21.126
"He already has a huge line of customers at the food truck."

58
00:03:22.527 --> 00:03:23.667
"Excuse me."

59
00:03:24.407 --> 00:03:27.068
A woman with long purple hair walked up to the counter.

60
00:03:28.148 --> 00:03:30.790
"I couldn't help but overhear that you're short-staffed today.

61
00:03:31.631 --> 00:03:33.913
I'm a chef, passing through town as I head west.

62
00:03:34.373 --> 00:03:35.634
I'd be happy to help you out.

63
00:03:36.355 --> 00:03:39.117
I've already eaten my breakfast, and I was impressed.

64
00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:41.079
It was delicious!"

65
00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.422
Ray looked at all the orders waiting to be filled.

66
00:03:45.442 --> 00:03:48.365
"Can you work a grill?"

67
00:03:48.705 --> 00:03:49.646
he asked hopefully.

68
00:03:49.666 --> 00:03:52.888
"Better than most back east," she replied.

69
00:03:52.908 --> 00:03:54.410
"What's your name?"

70
00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:55.371
Ray asked.

71
00:03:57.772 --> 00:03:59.854
"Melanie." "Then come on back to the kitchen, please, Melanie!"

72
00:04:00.294 --> 00:04:00.774
Ray said.

73
00:04:02.956 --> 00:04:04.758
Finally, it was the end of the day.

74
00:04:06.059 --> 00:04:10.882
The diner was empty, and Ally, Flo, Ray, and Melanie were having a cold drink.

75
00:04:10.902 --> 00:04:14.866
"Phew! My feet are tired!"

76
00:04:15.506 --> 00:04:17.388
Flo flopped down onto a stool.

77
00:04:17.408 --> 00:04:18.949
"So are my hands!"

78
00:04:19.489 --> 00:04:19.930
Ray said.

79
00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:24.033
"I can't remember the last time I flipped so many burgers in one day."

80
00:04:24.053 --> 00:04:27.696
"You're a pretty fast flipper," Melanie said.

81
00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.561
"You're not bad yourself."

82
00:04:30.062 --> 00:04:30.702
Ray smiled.

83
00:04:30.722 --> 00:04:32.724
"Seriously, thank you.

84
00:04:33.285 --> 00:04:35.527
I couldn't have gotten through the day without your help."

85
00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:40.231
"I'm happy to come back tomorrow too if you need help," Melanie said.

86
00:04:40.251 --> 00:04:42.913
"That would be great," Ray said.

87
00:04:42.933 --> 00:04:47.437
"The food truck is booked at a carnival for the next two days, so I'll be without my

88
00:04:47.477 --> 00:04:47.958
cook again."

89
00:04:47.978 --> 00:04:49.720
"No worries."

90
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.582
Melanie grabbed her backpack from behind the counter.

91
00:04:52.602 --> 00:04:54.324
"I'll see you in the morning."

92
00:05:00.256 --> 00:05:03.777
"What luck," Flo said after Melanie had left.

93
00:05:03.797 --> 00:05:05.738
"She saved the day."

94
00:05:06.378 --> 00:05:07.718
Mateo had just entered.

95
00:05:07.738 --> 00:05:09.699
"Did somebody say 'luck'?

96
00:05:10.659 --> 00:05:11.879
I wish I had some."

97
00:05:11.899 --> 00:05:14.420
"What's wrong, Mateo?"

98
00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:15.340
Ally asked.

99
00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:19.401
"You look like you lost your best friend," Flo said.

100
00:05:19.421 --> 00:05:21.862
"Well, he did.

101
00:05:22.262 --> 00:05:24.803
Bethany is still out of town," Ally said.

102
00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:27.583
"No, it's not that."

103
00:05:28.224 --> 00:05:29.244
Mateo sat down.

104
00:05:30.336 --> 00:05:36.901
"Someone calling themselves UserPFM5 keeps outbidding me for the first Cosmic Quest comic.

105
00:05:37.621 --> 00:05:39.523
And the auction ends really soon."

106
00:05:39.543 --> 00:05:42.745
"That's terrible," Ally said.

107
00:05:42.765 --> 00:05:44.726
"What can you do about it?"

108
00:05:44.746 --> 00:05:48.329
"Only one thing," Mateo said.

109
00:05:48.349 --> 00:05:50.731
"Keep bidding until the bitter
